put dolby vision audio on the video clock

In a Dolby Vision recording (mm/DV, classes7) the audio samples reach MediaMuxer.writeSampleData with CLOCK_BOOTTIME
timestamps and the video frames with CLOCK_MONOTONIC ones. Once the phone has slept the two differ by the total sleep
time, MPEG4Writer gives the audio track an empty edit of that length, and players report a duration of hours
(VID20261021173522.mp4: audio start 151356.66 s, boottime - monotonic on the phone 151356.7 s). The muxer
(mm/i.writeSampleData) has already subtracted the first video key frame time from every sample when DV.sample()
sees it, so a correct audio timestamp is near 0 and a boot-clock one near the clock gap. DV.sample() now shifts each
audio sample of a Dolby Vision recording by that gap when the recorder's first audio timestamp is nearer the gap
than 0. Source: .claude/tools/cam7/dolby/mm/DV.java.

